{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db","id":833349,"title":"Narrative Logistics for a Lunar Impersonating a DB?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-19T09:41:32-08:00","id":833349,"title":"Narrative Logistics for a Lunar Impersonating a DB?","content":"So I'm looking to have a Lunar NPC show up in my campaign soon, who's masquerading as a known DB. By which I mean she has stolen a DB's identity and has been living it long-term. What are the sorts of narrative hurdles she might have to face, and possible solutions for them? I'm not looking for mechanics exactly, as I am willing to hand-wave them for the sake of story. Any help with the idea would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> So what I have so far is that she probably has artifact weapons with elemental flavor. Probably the volcano cutter.<br /> <br /> The sorcerous tell for Stormwind Rider would be helpful, if there was a flame version for it. Does Magma Kraken have a flamey tell? I'll look that up later.<br /> <br /> Continuing down the sorcerous route, I'm thinking she'll have Workings tied into a couple items that help her emulate anima flux. She'll still have to control her emotions, since outbursts should lead to more fluxing, but having things randomly burst into flames should be doable.<br /> <br /> How might she emulate some iconic DB charms? More artifacts? What would be the ones that she absolutely must be able to approximate to pull this off?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1990_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1990\" data-vbnamecard=\"1990\">norraba</a> , I know you're going to read this. That's fine. It's not for you. You can participate in the conversation, just Keep it hush hush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1067,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1067-primefactorx01","user":"Primefactorx01","date":". 02-19-2016, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1067-primefactorx01","name":"Primefactorx01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:16:22-08:00","id":833364,"title":"","content":"Step 1: Get item that renders wearer immune to fire<br /> Step 2: Set self on fire.<br /> <br /> <br /> In seriousness, it's fairly easy to trick mortals. You can always just warn them that your awesome Exalted powers aren't to be wasted on frivolous things. Cultivate a legend of marshaling your strength like Hessiesh. If you know what aspect the DB is, you might be able to simulate certain elemental features with shapeshifting small facets. <br /> <br /> The anima is the tricky part of course. Second edition straight up had a stone that mimicked a fire aspects anima for double the mote costs. <br /> <br /> Not really sure what could help the duplication of that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:20:46-08:00","id":833369,"title":"","content":"Disguise of a new face. <br /> <br /> Won't give you Anima Flux, but you will look the part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:49:12-08:00","id":833385,"title":"","content":"There's nothing she &quot;has&quot; to approximate beyond looking like the person and acting the part. Nobody is going to go up to her and say &quot;prove who you say you are using Elemental Bolt or I'll assume I'm actually talking to a shapeshifting demon!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> And if someone DOES do that, any DB worth their salt would just beat the shit out of whoever dared talk to them like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:21:01-08:00","id":833398,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm actually having her impersonate a Realm DB. I imagine she's going into seclusion for obvious reasons, but I figure she is going to have to interact with other DBs, at least on occasion. Which I imagine is where issues might arise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1067-primefactorx01","name":"Primefactorx01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:23:28-08:00","id":833401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primefactorx01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833398#post833398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm actually having her impersonate a Realm DB. I imagine she's going into seclusion for obvious reasons, but I figure she is going to have to interact with other DBs, at least on occasion. Which I imagine is where issues might arise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With other Realm DB, it's less DB powers and more Social Engineering. The Lunar will have to know the Realm pretty well to pull off the impersonation in front of Dragonblooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:41:16-08:00","id":833414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833401#post833401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With other Realm DB, it's less DB powers and more Social Engineering. The Lunar will have to know the Realm pretty well to pull off the impersonation in front of Dragonblooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. <br /> <br /> I generally assume DBs are smart with Essence use and use personal on Charms whenever possible to not give away that they are actually using Charms. Because obviously using charms can be socially detrimental at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:46:59-08:00","id":833421,"title":"","content":"I don't know how set your background is for this NPC, but you could have the Lunar come from the Realm and ran off after they Exalted as a Lunar. That way they know the Realm just like a Native, though their information could be out of date.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:49:14-08:00","id":833424,"title":"","content":"If it's an option you could have the Lunar pretend to be an Outcaste or Lost Egg or whatever they call them. That way you have an excuse to not know the Realm/have barbaric manners. Also, there continues to be nothing Burning Name can't solve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:59:45-08:00","id":833504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primefactorx01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db#post833349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sorcerous tell for Stormwind Rider would be helpful, if there was a flame version for it. Does Magma Kraken have a flamey tell? I'll look that up later..</div> </div> </div> </div>Magma Kraken as a control causes the person to be chased by magma fire, occasionally little bits of fire will answer their needs in little ways like the book mentions a tentacle of fire coming from a torch to light the person's pipe for them. <br /> <br /> As has been said most of the time this Lunar will probably have more problems with just having knowledge and acting as one of the DBs would. Just being a good fighter will handle most of the power issues because unless the person is known for crap like throwing out elemental bolts at the drop of a hat what will they complain about? Probably the trickiest part will be mimicking the moodiness that tends to crop up with DBs since it might be a bit of a pain to act like a boisterous hot head if the lunar's personality is more calm and not big on being the center of attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T15:06:00-08:00","id":833547,"title":"","content":"There is a fire aspected hearthstone (we are talking a 2nd ed game here right?) that gives you a 'fake' fire DB anima you can pop at-will. That'll go a hell of a long way to prove that you're a DB.<br /> <br /> Some kind of custom shapeshifting knack that 'shapeshifts' your essence as well - so anyone who looks at you with essence sight seeks the right flavor of elemental essence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:19:39-08:00","id":833569,"title":"","content":"Things are gonna be tough. I think you'll need to restrict the character cleverly to situations where Charms are internal or you plausibly wouldn't want to use them. Sorcerous workings and borrowed magic from spirits seem like the least blatant way to fake Dragonblooded elemental power, but I think people will know if they look close (audience dependent: faking a DB to Solars - probably not as hard; to DBs - well, IMO not much easier than faking being a Lunar as a Dragonblooded or Sidereal to another Lunar). If the character can have allies who've helped her prepare all this in the background (and are maybe now out of the picture) that will make it easier without the character herself needing that much sorcerous capability.<br /> <br /> Edit: In general, I think Lunars have it easier pretending to be some Exigent or strange god or behemoth or god blooded. Faking being a standard Exalt is hard, because they're relatively standardised as sub splats (so it's weird if they can't do some particular capability universal to the Exalt) and have a lot of separate ways to express their underlying power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 02-19-2016, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:00:35-08:00","id":833618,"title":"","content":"Get a Hearthstone that gives you effects to mimic the anima. That's the hardest part. If you're in 3E, get the ST to let you use one of the hearthstones that gives you an ice-aura or a fire aura or lets you breathe water.<br /> <br /> Social stuff is easy if you're a social kind of Lunar. Learn some Immaculate martial arts just to be on the safe side-DBs won't call you out for not using DB charms in a pinch if you're using those, because DBs use them in a pinch!<br /> <br /> If you're claiming to be a DB you ate, and you look like her and you sound like her and you act like her, nobody is going to ASSUME she's been eaten by a face-stealing demon-monster since last time she was over for tea. You don't think that about your friends! If you're acting a little off, the default assumption isn't going to be &quot;IT MUST BE AN ANATHEMA,&quot; it's going to be &quot;I wonder if she's feeling stressed,&quot; or &quot;is she ill,&quot; or &quot;did I do something to offend her?&quot;<br /> <br /> We don't assume people we know have been replaced by horrible monsters wearing their skins all the time in real life, after all!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:19:08-08:00","id":833624,"title":"","content":"So I assume it's a Fire Aspect.<br /> <br /> Have the Ifrit initiation so you can shoot fire.<br /> Learn the Lunar charm that makes you immune to fire.<br /> That'll go some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:35:14-08:00","id":833635,"title":"","content":"People have covered anima banners and charms pretty well, so I'm going to focus on what makes one a <i>dynast</i>, rather than a Dragon Blooded, which, IMO, is the immensely harder and more interesting con to pull off. These are all potential complications - how well the lunar handled them, how much they came up, etc, are obviously up to you.<br /> <br /> <b>Retainers</b>. Dynasts are <i>never </i>alone. You know all those personally loyal close friends of your victims? Are you good enough to fool them? Are you sure? It might be best to arrange their accidental deaths at the same time you take over your new role - excellent excuse to be in mourning for a while, and changed afterwards.<br /> <br /> <b>Family</b>.Did you remember to get your nephew an exaltation gift? Shame you killed off your retainer (who was getting too suspicious) before he remembered to remind you. And your Grand Aunt's 150th coming up - do you recall that she doesn't like red jade, reminds her too much of that incident fifteen years ago, and also that you can't get her another dress, because you did that last year? No one will tell you these things - seriously, they won't. You're supposed to already know.<br /> <br /> <b>Responsibility</b>. Every dynast has something they were doing before you replaced them. Sure you're going into seclusion, but before you go, we could <i>reaaaaly </i>use a rundown on how to keep things going while you're gone. Like, you ordered three months of beer for the troops but nothing else - I assume you had a deal lined up, a trade with someone to cover that, really, I'm sure it's brilliant, but you need to tell me before you leave or we'll have soldiers with beer and nothing to eat, and that sounds perfectly stable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T19:04:17-08:00","id":833649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833385#post833385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing she &quot;has&quot; to approximate beyond looking like the person and acting the part. Nobody is going to go up to her and say &quot;prove who you say you are using Elemental Bolt or I'll assume I'm actually talking to a shapeshifting demon!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> And if someone DOES do that, any DB worth their salt would just beat the shit out of whoever dared talk to them like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This always struck me as really weird. I mean for fifteen centuries, your greatest enemy has been a band of murderous skinwalkers who could fool your own mother by killing you and eating your heart, and you're gonna get pissy about identity checks? It's like the Realm's security protocols were designed by Wes Craven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T19:39:48-08:00","id":833665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833649#post833649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This always struck me as really weird. I mean for fifteen centuries, your greatest enemy has been a band of murderous skinwalkers who could fool your own mother by killing you and eating your heart, and you're gonna get pissy about identity checks? It's like the Realm's security protocols were designed by Wes Craven.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the circumstances. I mean if you're in an area where lunar activity is almost constant then yeah anyone gone for a significant amount of time or who goes missing will likely be asked to verify that they are really who they say they are. At the same time though, you could only have it be so extreme before it starts causing problems. I mean, &quot;Hey look you were gone a while and we've had reports of anathema shapeshifters nearby it would really put everyone's mind at ease if you could flare up a bit to verify you didn't get switched.&quot; Would certainly be a fair thing to ask a DB who's been out most of the day, but it doesn't work for mortals. It would just be absurd if years later someone ambushes them after they wake up in the morning demanding they prove their identity if there is no reason to suspect they were taken beyond the fact that lunars exist and it could maybe have happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T19:49:38-08:00","id":833668,"title":"","content":"I imagine that for the Wyld Hunt, checks are routine and demanded. For dynasts just hanging out with their families, they don't bother, because... well, everyone's throwing Socialise and Investigation charms around all the time, because intrigue, anyway.<br /> <br /> For places like war manses, routine checks are probably the case, just like in real world military installations.<br /> <br /> So, if you're not going to any sensitive places, your main issues are going to be defending against people constantly using DB charms to find out your intimacies. They're expecting to find out which political faction you're in, who you're sleeping with, and who you're hating, but if they discover that you have Major intimacies of &quot;The Scarlet Dynasty - Abject Hatred&quot; and &quot;Lunars - My bros&quot;, that's pretty suspicious.<br /> <br /> Of course, in 2nd ed, what happened was they threw Revelation of Associate's Hunch at you and realised your friends are all Lunars. In 2.5... they throw Revelation of Associate's Hunch at you 4 or 5 times, and it keeps failing, which is possible against a DB but unlikely, so they get suspicious.<br /> Hopefully it won't really work like that in 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> I'd think a knack that lets you pretend to have the intimacies of the person you've eaten would be pretty reasonable, and essential for infiltrating the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T20:04:19-08:00","id":833673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833421#post833421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how set your background is for this NPC, but you could have the Lunar come from the Realm and ran off after they Exalted as a Lunar. That way they know the Realm just like a Native, though their information could be out of date.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833424#post833424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's an option you could have the Lunar pretend to be an Outcaste or Lost Egg or whatever they call them. That way you have an excuse to not know the Realm/have barbaric manners. Also, there continues to be nothing Burning Name can't solve.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lunar's background isn't set yet, but the Dynast she will be impersonating is already established in a character's backstory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833635#post833635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have covered anima banners and charms pretty well, so I'm going to focus on what makes one a <i>dynast</i>, rather than a Dragon Blooded, which, IMO, is the immensely harder and more interesting con to pull off. These are all potential complications - how well the lunar handled them, how much they came up, etc, are obviously up to you.<br /> <br /> <b>Retainers</b>. ...<br /> <br /> <b>Family</b>....<br /> <br /> <b>Responsibility</b>. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>All excellent points! Exactly the sort of thing I was looking for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1067-primefactorx01","name":"Primefactorx01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T20:13:56-08:00","id":833679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833668#post833668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that for the Wyld Hunt, checks are routine and demanded. For dynasts just hanging out with their families, they don't bother, because... well, everyone's throwing Socialise and Investigation charms around all the time, because intrigue, anyway.<br /> <br /> For places like war manses, routine checks are probably the case, just like in real world military installations.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a good chance she's going to be participating in something like a Wyld hunt, so I'll have to figure out how she'd get around that. Perhaps some elemental party trick that the original DB likes to do that no one else has figured out, that the Lunar is emulating with an item.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1067-primefactorx01","name":"Primefactorx01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T20:51:23-08:00","id":833689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primefactorx01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833679#post833679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a good chance she's going to be participating in something like a Wyld hunt, so I'll have to figure out how she'd get around that. Perhaps some elemental party trick that the original DB likes to do that no one else has figured out, that the Lunar is emulating with an item.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well how out of character would it be for the cover to act as a scout?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T09:54:53-08:00","id":833889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primefactorx01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833679#post833679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a good chance she's going to be participating in something like a Wyld hunt, so I'll have to figure out how she'd get around that. Perhaps some elemental party trick that the original DB likes to do that no one else has figured out, that the Lunar is emulating with an item.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be basing a lot of this disguise thing around &quot;the Lunar is going to need to be able to flare anima like a DB,&quot; which I consider to be a faulty premise, but having some kind of sorcerous working tied to wearing the DB's shape, and thereby having an anima that at least looks right that might also do superficial damage to the environment, would be the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T10:42:55-08:00","id":833912,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall a quote from Holden that said something like Lunars can <i>easily</i> infiltrate the Dynasty's social fabric... but that while DBs don't have the tools to locate them effectively, Sidereals <i>do</i>. It was pointed out as one of the main reasons the Bronze Faction is really helpful to the Realm, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T14:41:19-08:00","id":834061,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of social things that Dynasts do that could contribute to suspicion if not performed - a single one of these might not be enough on its own, but when it's consistently missed or ignored, <i>someone</i> might think to use an awareness or investigation charm our of curiosity.<br /> <br /> DBs attend and throw parties, they socialize, talk about business, finance, hunts, etc. If a DB suddenly stopped attending or throwing parties (such as because they were eaten by a Lunar and that Lunar doesn't know about the venues), someone will notice and confront the &quot;DB&quot; about their newfound rudeness.<br /> <br /> Likewise, forgetting important details about bloodlines and house politics (such as those that would be common knowledge to the dynasts) would also arouse interest, in the &quot;are you sure you're okay?&quot; way - examples might include completely ignoring courtiers or business ventures, forgetting the name of the children of your House's leader, forgetting your own lineage or crest.<br /> <br /> Dynasts are also expected to spend their wealth and treat humans like their lessers, operating through patricians to avoid getting their hands (literally and metaphorically) dirty. Mingling to closely with humans or taking too much of a hands-on approach might seem odd depending on one's background.<br /> <br /> Again, taken on their own, any one of these kinds of things are just a minor oddity; but as minor oddities pile on, the chances of someone checking up on you, potentially with charms (investigation, medicine, socialize) grows. It only takes someone legitimately concerned for your well-being for you to be discovered.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T09:44:04-08:00","id":835119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833649#post833649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This always struck me as really weird. I mean for fifteen centuries, your greatest enemy has been a band of murderous skinwalkers who could fool your own mother by killing you and eating your heart, and you're gonna get pissy about identity checks? It's like the Realm's security protocols were designed by Wes Craven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whose greatest allies are people with no past and no way to prove themselves who you just have this feeling you've known for some time. Lets say there are competing priorities about identity checks.<br /> <br /> Regarding things the Lunar could stumble upon, rather than solutions to overcome those challenges (because that's what player ingenuity is for!) here are some tripwires beyond 'Dynastic politics of the day', 'fooling Essence sight' or 'forgetting that friend that fell out of touch':<br /> 1.) A spirit using measure the wind and telling a Realm Dragon-Blooded you are trying to fool.<br /> 2.) A mother's love / father's pride. You have to fool possibly dozens of Essence-capbable people your target is related to.<br /> 3.) A Sidereal checking your strand of Fate. (I think 2e had a Knack to help with this)<br /> 4.) A Solar (maybe even Lyta!) who bring murderous prejudice against you while in disguise.<br /> 5.) A mountain-folk not honoring the contract 'you' made previously because some magic they have regarding contracts can tell you aren't who you claim to be.<br /> 6.) A demon your target had summoned going on a rampage due to the binding breaking and not repsonding to your commands because 'you' never bound it.<br /> 7.) Not being attuned to a Manse your target had been attuned to for decades.<br /> 8.) Not knowing how to [Ability] like your target did (Sail!)<br /> 9.) Your retainers who watch you daily begin to notice small inconsistencies.<br /> 10.) Being called up by a retrieval pack of Lunars who are confused why you can't take a few days off pretending to be a Dragon-Blooded to help a cub.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T11:08:50-08:00","id":835191,"title":"","content":"Someone stumbling across the corpse of your disguise. (I mean it may have been securely handled originally, but over the months stuff can happen. Like someone raising it as a zombie)<br /> If the lunar didn't handle burial rights properly then eventually you could get the fun of someone getting into a fight with the DBs hungry ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T20:54:34-08:00","id":836216,"title":"","content":"I want to say that, in 2e, Lunars had a charm that let them disguise their anima and charms as those of the type of being who's shape they had eaten. While I'm aware that Lunars probably aren't going to get to chow down on all sorts of gods and things in 3e, I don't really see why they wouldn't have charms to fake being another type of Exalt. Which seems like the easy answer to the problem at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:52:59-08:00","id":841360,"title":"","content":"In 2e the Lunar had to hunt their target for a day before taking their form. This meant that they learned about their target somewhat. With a target like this I'd recommend that the Lunar kill a lesser assistant to the DB to learn as much about them as possible for several months before taking their form. This would allow them to learn the target's schedule and intricate social details. As for hiding your type of powers, I seem to recall(but may be wrong) the lunar means of doing that required Essence 6 so that may not be available. The Hearthstone may work. In 2e the Martial Arts style Fivefold Shadow hand granted the practitioner an elemental aspect if they didn't already have one. If converted to 3e, this could potentially be used to enhance this disguise. I don't remember precisely, but i think the Immaculate styles could do this too. Even with all these techniques, they may have to contend with deep investigations which may require a quiet &quot;removal&quot; of said investigator and the creation of &quot;evidence&quot; that said investigator had been somehow affronted by the &quot;Dragon-Blooded&quot; in some way and was seeking revenge. Either way, prepare an escape route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T21:08:40-08:00","id":841697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/833349-narrative-logistics-for-a-lunar-impersonating-a-db?p=833618#post833618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't assume people we know have been replaced by horrible monsters wearing their skins all the time in real life, after all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Speak for yourself.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T22:31:34-08:00","id":841731,"title":"","content":"Actually Capgras delusion would be an interesting issue. I mean as we've stated not too hard for a DB to at least assuage the afflicted individual with a minor flare to show what they are, but I mean depending on how much of a threat Lunar infiltration was in the area a returning DB could be under some sort of therapy for cracking and assuming basically everyone is a fake. Hell if they know about Sids so much the worse for the individual. Actually be kind of an amusing cover for an infiltrator if you could swing it so you wouldn't just get locked up or something as a potential threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:20:50-08:00","id":842266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</str